    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SETUP & SECURITY (read before activating)\n\n**1. Credentials** - none are included. Open each Telegram / SSH / Gemini node and create your own.\n\n**2. Authorization gate** - open **If (only me)** and replace `YOUR_TELEGRAM_USER_ID` with your numeric Telegram ID (message @userinfobot). Until you do, the bot ignores EVERYONE (fail-closed). Never share the bot username publicly.\n\n**3. SSH** - use a **private key** credential, never a password. Create a dedicated low-privilege Linux user that can only read this repo and run python. Disable password login in sshd (`PasswordAuthentication no`).\n\n**4. Updates** - this workflow does NOT run `git pull`. Update the server's copy manually, after reviewing the changes. Auto-pulling means a hacked repo = code execution on your server.\n\n**5. Server path** - the commands assume the repo lives at `~/Macro-Quant-Lab`. Change it in both Execute nodes if yours differs.\n\n**6. Built-in limits** - 30 s cooldown between commands (works once the workflow is ACTIVE), scripts killed after 90 s, script failures stop the run, output capped, URLs stripped from replies. Set a spending cap on your Gemini key too.\n\n**7. Never** export this workflow again without removing credential IDs, webhook IDs and instance ID.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
